    "scope_note": "Covers both cross-check paths (full-frame and crop) and the crop decision. Species resolution, capture-time decoding and weather enrichment are also analytical, and are listed under column_classification.analytical_verdict.out_of_scope_for_verdict_digest rather than hashed here. They are excluded deliberately: none is re-run by recompute-crosscheck / recompute-crops / recompute-crop-crosscheck, and backfill-weather calls a live API whose response could differ for reasons unrelated to any refactor -- which would make the gate fail without a defect. Their distributions and per-species counts are recorded above as a separate check.",
    "how_it_is_computed": [
      "Absent columns are selected as SQL NULL, so a 52-column and a 90-column database produce comparably shaped rows and comparable digests.",
      "Field encoding: NULL -> JSON null; a float column -> a string formatted '%.6f'; a *_json column -> canonicalised (see below); everything else -> its string value.",
      "Rows are sorted ascending by source_message_id using Python's default str ordering (Unicode code point), NOT SQLite's collation.",
      "Each row is serialised as a JSON array with json.dumps(row, ensure_ascii=False, separators=(',',':')).",
      "SHA-256 over the concatenation of those lines, each followed by a single b'\\n'. Hex digest, lowercase."
    ]
