  "shared_encoding_rationale": {
    "why_floats_are_rounded": "Fixed 6dp formatting makes the digests reproducible across platforms and BLAS builds, where a last-bit difference carries no analytical meaning. A change large enough to matter at IoU or score scale is far above 1e-6, and the full-precision min/max/mean/quartiles in 'numeric_summaries' remain available as a second, finer check.",
    "null_representation": "JSON null. Chosen over a sentinel string because no stored value can collide with it -- a literal '<NULL>' in the data could."
